Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||04-01-2001||01:03 AM||||i think i remember someone posting about keith huff putting a 4.11 final drive gear in a 5 speed- anyone have info about that? that would be cool! i have an 87gt, what would i need to do to add this gear to my 5 speed getrag?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PJ||04-01-2001||11:57 AM||||I don't know about a 4.11 but you can put a 3.94 in there. I've done it. I think Rodney has a lot of info on this on his site.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||04-01-2001||01:10 PM||||Hey PJ how much different does the 3.94 gears feel and drive compared to the 3.61 gears? Did they improve your 0-60 times and quarter miles times compared to the 3.61 gears? What engine modifications do you have or is your engine stock?<P>I have a computer simulation program that can pretty accurately predict this information but I always like to get feedback from real experiences.<P>Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||04-01-2001||05:12 PM||||Mantaparts.com has a 4.11 final drive for the Isuzu 5-speed.  They also have the 3.94 for the Getrag.||||reg||1
Z||000004||PJ||04-01-2001||09:22 PM||||I've never run a timed 1/4 mi. or 0-60 so I can't say. I do race the car on road courses though. With the 3.61 the motor wouldn't spin past 5,500rpm in fourth. Fifth gear was useless, even with 205/50 15's on the rear you'd lose too many rpm's shifting up. With the 3.94 and 225/50's on the rear I can hit the limiter at 6,500rpm in fourth and get up to about 5,500rpm in fifth. With the torque of the 2.8L and the shorter final the car squirts out of the corners better also.<BR>The rules for the class the car is in prohibit almost all engine mods so it is basically stock - at least it looks and sounds like its stock.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||3400Fiero||04-02-2001||01:35 PM||||What's the web site address again?  I tried mantaparts.com and it didn't work.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC||||reg||5
Z||000006||Will||04-02-2001||02:29 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.mantapart.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mantapart.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||04-03-2001||02:54 AM||||Keith Huff put the 4.10 gears from an 84 4 speed tranny into an 86 SE 4 speed tranny.<P>He did this because he did not trust the reliabilty of the 84 tranny case. We had seen an 84 tranny case that had been put on an 86 GT come into the shop in pieces. They guy beat it up and then blew it up. Since the 4.10 gears were going to have a 3.4 motivation, the tranny originaly hooked up to the V6 seemed to be the reliable choice.<P>4.10s in a 5 speed...now that would be interesting!||||reg||6
Z||000008||lou_dias||04-03-2001||09:13 AM||||I think <A HREF="http://www.isuzuperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.isuzuperformance.com</A>  sells differentials for our transmissions...||||reg||1
